Cell[TextData[{
 "This formula describes the overall substrate turnover under the assumption \
that each of the successive substrate binding events may have different \
binding affinities, and that each occupancy state may display a different \
catalytic constant. \nNote that if n=1 or all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["K", 
    RowBox[{"S", ",", "i"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5375eab6-5a52-49ec-9d60-e1e1f60dce1c"],
 " are equal, the equation reduces to the Henri-Michaelis-Menten equation. \
This is the situation of absence of cooperativity and means that an oligomer \
behaves as a mixture of n independent enzymes. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJwdzU0og3EAx/HlhsyW2bSkHGxtaaHcpu1pscJKO6CJ1QxzmGlFM+2Acpm2
sqWVi93UxDCnIYdlL4nVXmLzsnaYejArVlaS/2+Hb5/jt11nUs/UMBgMPgmW
