Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 2: Substrate binding and dissociation to an enzyme with four binding \
pockets. The second substrate can be bound to either of the three remaining, \
free sites, giving raise to three possible forward reactions. The previous \
state (one substrate bound) can be reached by dissociation of either of the \
two ligands, i.e. from each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"E", "\[CenterDot]", 
    SubscriptBox["S", "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "298a87f8-9e5d-4c15-807c-f5ce6c46e4cc"],
 "state, there are two reverse paths. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.694872740308818*^9, 3.6948727448521557`*^9}, {
  3.6957093723811617`*^9, 3.695709374212212*^9}, {3.719734374662339*^9, 
  3.719734376021804*^9}, {3.719734461352054*^9, 3.7197345010258083`*^9}, {
  3.71973469493864*^9, 3.719734835727325*^9}},
 Background->GrayLevel[
  0.85],ExpressionUUID->"416609b4-457e-4d52-bb33-06522a2e30f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Analogous as before, we find that there are ",
 StyleBox["three",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " possibilities to occupy another substrate binding site, and from each of \
the resulting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"E", "\[CenterDot]", 
    SubscriptBox["S", "2"], " "}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3998aa86-f3b9-4602-95d9-aa94c3de7864"],
 "complexes,there are ",
 StyleBox["two",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ways of loosing one ligand. Hence, "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.52939199545092*^9, 3.529392030385601*^9}, {
   3.529909363754841*^9, 3.529909401998101*^9}, {3.529992957650943*^9, 
   3.529993012770917*^9}, {3.529995036438624*^9, 3.5299950664333878`*^9}, {
   3.5299956450261297`*^9, 3.5299956528722*^9}, {3.530016100214006*^9, 
   3.530016113181623*^9}, {3.5302571831145782`*^9, 3.53025719316399*^9}, {
   3.53036011691924*^9, 3.53036011940478*^9}, {3.530360453091729*^9, 
   3.530360611171649*^9}, {3.530379943470376*^9, 3.5303800028199787`*^9}, 
   3.530380049474375*^9, {3.5304204369225693`*^9, 3.530420443651127*^9}, {
   3.530420964695087*^9, 3.530421044946576*^9}, 3.530421115587619*^9, {
   3.5304213538128147`*^9, 3.530421425579742*^9}, 3.530433511343391*^9, {
   3.719728445092225*^9, 3.71972846077317*^9}, {3.719728499428377*^9, 
   3.71972861292253*^9}, {3.7197306208621483`*^9, 3.719730624299616*^9}, {
   3.719730660736299*^9, 3.7197306670214233`*^9}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 1, 0.85],ExpressionUUID->"5d79e3ad-bd66-496e-a749-1273b8d5fe66"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["K", 
    RowBox[{"S", ",", "2"}]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"3", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["k", "23"]}], 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["k", "32"]}]]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.719728474723648*^9, 3.719728494084279*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[36]:=",ExpressionUUID->"92bd0ee1-81ec-4456-b50a-3bc93bad0ba7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the third and forth binding step, the combinatorics is as follows, \
showing ",
 StyleBox["two",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (",
 StyleBox["one",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ") path forward from 2\[LongRightArrow]3 (3\[LongRightArrow]4) ligands, and ",
 StyleBox["three",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (",
 StyleBox["four",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", respectivly) ways back:\n",
